Add a runtime classic-AirPlay-only mode to the AirPlay 2 build

general.airplay_classic_only makes an AirPlay-2-capable build
advertise and serve classic AirPlay exclusively: the _airplay._tcp
service is not registered (NULL secondary records - the exact shape
the shared mdns code already handles for classic-only builds), and
the _raop._tcp record set switches to the classic-build one, whose
records carry no ft= AirPlay 2 feature bits, so senders negotiate
classic AirPlay.

Why anyone would want this: the receiver-side remote control channel
(DACP) only exists for classic sessions - modern iOS runs no DACP
server for AirPlay 2 (see mikebrady/shairport-sync#2186; the AP2
control channel is encrypted and not reverse engineered), so a
speaker with its own transport buttons faces a trade: AirPlay 2
multi-room OR working play/pause/next from the speaker. This makes
the trade a config option. Off by default.

Group-status mdns updates are suppressed centrally in mdns_update so
the unregistered AP2 service is never updated.

Companion to 0001/0002; carried locally by boompi.

